G3D: the App-facing helpers PLAYER calls out of line, as upstream G3D declares them (g3d SVN r30
G3D.lib/include/G3D/{Matrix3,Vector3,Vector2,CoordinateFrame}.h; bodies from r30 source/*.cpp). The
2016 fork inlined them in the headers. PLAYER evidence (calls from Roblox code outside the G3D block
0x009d5b70-0x009edf00, tools/lib/g3d_calls.py):
  Matrix3::Matrix3(const Matrix3&)  0x009d7f30 (folded with Matrix3(const float[3][3]): rep movsd, ret 4),
                                    315 calls in 237 functions, e.g. PartInstance::setCoordinateFrame
                                    0x00725487; Matrix3::operator= stays inline (memcpy -> rep movsd at
                                    0x007254de in the same function)
  Matrix3::zero 0x009d9330, identity 0x009d93a0 (62 calls in 53 functions)
  Vector3::zero 0x009da920 (271 calls in 151 functions), one 0x009da960, unitX 0x009da9a0,
          unitY 0x009da9e0, unitZ 0x009daa20, inf and nan 0x009daa60 (folded: finf and fnan fold),
          minFinite 0x009daae0 (-FLT_MAX), maxFinite 0x009dab20 (FLT_MAX), in upstream Vector3.cpp order
  Vector2::one 0x009d6a60, zero 0x009d6aa0 (64 calls in 46 functions)
  CoordinateFrame::CoordinateFrame() 0x009d9550 (160 calls in 130 functions): identity(), Matrix3 copy
                                    ctor, zero().
G3D-side result (tools/lib/g3d_match.py, PLAYER): 153 -> 174 identical; all of the above become identical,
and CoordinateFrame::lookAt (both overloads), lerp, Quat::toRotationMatrix, Ray::set and Box::init, which
inlined the old header bodies, become identical too.

